Andrea Schulman is an accomplished educational leader with over 15 years of experience in Jewish education, curriculum development, and youth programming. Currently serving as the Director of Women's Missions, Shidduchim, Parent Programming & Recruiting at Aish in Jerusalem, Israel, she expertly organizes and leads adult women's missions while developing comprehensive educational programming and trip coordination.

With a Master's in Education and Bachelor's in Psychology from the City University of New York, Andrea brings both academic rigor and practical expertise to her diverse roles. She has been the Director of Chinuch at Camp Dina in Pennsylvania since 2015, where she hires, trains, and supervises staff while creating innovative educational programming including shiur programs and daily thematic lessons.

Andrea's multifaceted career spans various educational settings, from her role as a Mechaneches and Tanach teacher at Midreshet Shalhevet (2009-2019) to her current position as an English Studies teacher at Bnos Bais Yaakov. She specializes in mentorship and training, demonstrating exceptional ability in relationship building with students, parents, and staff members.

As a Kallah teacher since 2018, Andrea teaches Halachos of Taharas Hamishpacha to women preparing for marriage, while also serving as an adult educator leading bi-weekly discussions on "Technology and its effect on our homes." Her bilingual capabilities in English and Hebrew, combined with her seminary training at Michlala in Jerusalem, enable her to connect with diverse audiences across cultural and educational contexts.

Andrea's proven track record includes organizing large-scale missions, recruiting and training educational staff, developing curricula, and creating meaningful virtual and in-person engagement opportunities. Her expertise in youth program direction and educational leadership makes her a sought-after professional in the Jewish educational community.